Build a single-file, scroll-driven product website for YEWALE AMRUTTULYA, a real tea chain from Pune, India (since 1983, 650+ outlets in 13 states). INSPIRED BY the SUNFIZZ / MotionSites soda site — same scroll-film architecture, same choreography language — but this is Yewale's own site, not a copy: the product is a 3D CUTTING CHAI GLASS (not a bottle), the palette is Yewale's red/cream/brown, the story is Yewale's real story, and — unlike SUNFIZZ — the page ends with a REAL MENU WITH PRICES, because that is the whole point of this preview. All products are real-time 3D chai glasses rendered with Three.js r160 on one full-screen WebGL canvas. Four story sections are choreographed on one continuous scroll timeline: hero carousel, sticky back-band story, manifesto, and a receding glass lineup. Every visible layer in the film is `position: fixed` and driven by a smoothed scroll value. The film runs over an empty 705vh tall track; after it ends, the canvas fades out and the page continues into normal scrolling sections (menu, signatures, story, outlets, contact, footer — see section 11).

